keywords:
  - jacobian-conjecture
  - deficiency-indices
  - essential-self-adjointness
  - exotic-ccr
abstract: >-
  Proposed, untagged targeted revision of the A001 paper package. For the
  canonical real dual transport operator H=-i X_1 associated with the
  restated Alpoge-Fable Keller seed, the paper gives Hilbert deficiency
  indices n_+=n_-=aleph0. The revised main proof constructs the minus-i
  family from a forward maximal sheet and obtains the plus-i family through
  the measure-preserving sign involution. The theorem-source root of the
  companion Lean artifact is ff50f4a2a312591c2e5b26e71eb390ade9164b34;
  its synchronized repository snapshot is
  94351f38d7d84fd073db14ff8764708fa9d2942b. These are not a final immutable
  release: a new single-SHA Lean freeze, fresh scientific and package gates,
  and Dan approval remain pending. Lean proves the exact aleph0 Hilbert-basis
  indices, the bounded canonical-core Theorems E-F, a bijective von Neumann
  classification for the specific H_X1_min, and at least two distinct
  self-adjoint-extension witnesses. No preferred extension, arbitrary-operator
  theorem, exact Hamel rank, exact extension cardinality, strong CCR, physical
  selection, or rank-three Dixmier counterexample is claimed. The backward
  wall is retained as independent paper geometry and is not used in the main
  deficiency proof. Prior withdrawn claims remain documented in the erratum.
